From: hamza <hamza@book4>
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] phy: qcom-mipi-csi2: drop unbalanced probe clock enable

The probe function prepares and enables every PHY clock, but never drops
that reference, either after registration or on subsequent probe failures.
The power_on/power_off pair takes and releases a separate reference, so a
streaming cycle cannot remove the original one. The driver also has no PM
callbacks which release these probe-time references during system suspend.

On the Book4, the two idle CSI PHYs retain their CSIPHY and timer clocks,
plus shared camera AHB/AXI references, while CAMSS is runtime-suspended.
These clocks descend from the sleep-inclusive XO clock.

Probe does not access PHY registers and does not need these clocks enabled.
Leave clock ownership to the existing power_on/power_off operations, which
enable clocks before reading the hardware version and configuring lanes.
The existing camera diagnostic patch does not add this probe enable.

Validation:
- Extracted-helper cycles and regulator/rate/clock failure checks passed
- Native module build and boot passed
- Camera captures before and after real suspend passed
- Idle clock release after normal CCI autosuspend verified
- Energy benefit unresolved
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-mipi-csi2-core.c | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-mipi-csi2-core.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-mipi-csi2-core.c
index 1def2d125..9161e6822 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-mipi-csi2-core.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-mipi-csi2-core.c
@@ -217,12 +217,6 @@ static int phy_qcom_mipi_csi2_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	ret = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(num_clk, csi2phy->clks);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "apq8016 clk_enable failed\n");
-		return ret;
-	}
-
 	num_supplies = csi2phy->soc_cfg->num_supplies;
 	csi2phy->supplies = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*csi2phy->supplies) * num_supplies,
 					 GFP_KERNEL);
